    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Polite imperative",
     "texto": [
      "To address someone politely, use forms such as **Fale** (speak), **Espere** (wait), **Venha** (come) and **Diga** (say).",
      "With **-ar**, it ends in **-e**: **falar → fale**. With many verbs in **-er/-ir**, it ends in **-a**: **comer → coma**, **abrir → abra**. The verb usually agrees in the third person."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Common forms",
     "texto": [
      "**Ser → seja**, **ir → vá**, **vir → venha**, **dizer → diga**.",
      "**Vá** is written with an accent; learn the full form **ir → vá**. To make the request sound polite, you can add **por favor** (please) or **se faz favor** (please)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
